      "amount": "1/4 cup"
    },
    {
      "name": "salt",
      "amount": "1/4 teaspoon"
    },
    {
      "name": "pepper",
      "amount": "1/2 teaspoon"
    },
    {
      "name": "vegetable oil",
      "amount": "1 cup"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "In a large bowl, mix together oats, onion, garlic, eggs, milk, flour, salt, and pepper until well combined.",
    "Heat about 1/2 inch of vegetable oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.",
    "Using a 1/4 cup measuring cup, scoop out the oats mixture and drop into the hot oil.",
    "Fry for 3-4 minutes on each side, or until golden brown and crispy.",
    "Drain the fritters on paper towels and serve hot.",
    "Serve warm and enjoy!",
    "Note: Be careful when working with hot oil."
